**Selenium 4 automatically manages drivers:**

```java
// Chrome
WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

// Firefox
WebDriver driver = new FirefoxDriver();

// Edge
WebDriver driver = new EdgeDriver();

// Safari (Mac only)
WebDriver driver = new SafariDriver();
```

**No need for:**
- ❌ System.setProperty() for driver paths
- ❌ Manual driver downloads
- ❌ WebDriverManager (though still useful for version management)

**Selenium Manager (since 4.6):**
- Automatically downloads correct driver version
- Matches browser version installed on system
- Caches drivers for reuse

**Best Practice:** Use WebDriverManager for fine-grained control in enterprise frameworks.

